{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 49,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear this, all ye peoples;\nGive ear, all ye inhabitants of the world,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Both low and high,\nRich and poor together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My mouth shall speak wisdom;\nAnd the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will incline mine ear to a parable:\nI will open my dark saying upon the harp.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil,\nWhen iniquity at my heels compasseth me about?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that trust in their wealth,\nAnd boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "None ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " can by any means redeem his brother,\nNor give to God a ransom for him",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For the redemption of their life is costly,\nAnd it faileth for ever),",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That he should still live alway,\nThat he should not see corruption.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he shall see it. Wise men die;\nThe fool and the brutish alike perish,\nAnd leave their wealth to others.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their inward thought is, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their houses ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall continue",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for ever,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their dwelling-places to all generations;\nThey call their lands after their own names.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in honor abideth not:\nHe is like the beasts that perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This their way is their folly:\nYet after them men approve their sayings. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are appointed as a flock for Sheol;\nDeath shall be their shepherd:\nAnd the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning;\nAnd their beauty shall be for Sheol to consume,\nThat there be no habitation for it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But God will redeem my soul from the power of Sheol;\nFor he will receive me. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not thou afraid when one is made rich,\nWhen the glory of his house is increased:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away;\nHis glory shall not descend after him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though while he lived he blessed his soul\n(And men praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself),",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall go to the generation of his fathers;They shall never see the light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.49.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Man that is in honor, and understandeth not,\nIs like the beasts that perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "The folly of trusting in riches.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of the sons of Korah.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
